/-!
# Complete centralizer table for the 9-point calculation

Each integer encodes the images of a permutation as base-9 digits. Lean checks
both inverse identities, even sign, commutation, and distinctness. The known
centralizer order then proves exhaustiveness. Involution and support tests select exactly
the two ambient alternating-group conjugacy classes, using the odd-centralizer
argument of `Basic` and `cycleType_replicate_two_iff`. The large arrays are
stored in blocks of 32 to keep kernel reduction small.

The tables were generated by `source/Generate.py`; no generator assertion is
used without a kernel proof. Source motivation: Aschbacher, “A 2-local
characterization of M12”, Proposition 3.3, p.38.
-/

